From 05da63cdf6fcbec44176b07d10cb5b5f75f5f1cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nieyin345 <nieyin0703@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:38:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(docs): reshell the chrome in Mcode's design tokens

The Docs renderer carries a full Word-style ribbon whose colours come from
GenOffice's semantic token layer. Mcode's shell is Claude-styled, and the two
read as two different products bolted together.

GenOffice already forbids raw colours in renderer CSS (check-theme-colors.mjs)
and routes every piece of chrome through packages/ui/src/tokens.css, so the
shell can be replaced by re-pointing those tokens rather than touching any
component. This adds apps/docs/src/renderer/mcode-theme.css, which overrides
the chrome tokens with Mcode's CDS ramp, and loads it from main.tsx only when
window.desktop exists - standalone GenOffice keeps its own Word visual.

Scope is deliberately narrow:

- Component tree, editor kernel, ProseMirror schema, document model, save and
  export paths are untouched.
- Per-app brand accents (--accent, --word-blue) are not overridden: they stay
  the app's own.
- Word-semantic colours (revision bar, search hits) are not overridden: they
  tell the user which Word construct they are looking at.
- Document content colours never live in the token layer and are not touched.
---
 apps/docs/src/renderer/main.tsx        |   6 +
 apps/docs/src/renderer/mcode-theme.css | 235 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 241 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 apps/docs/src/renderer/mcode-theme.css

diff --git a/apps/docs/src/renderer/main.tsx b/apps/docs/src/renderer/main.tsx
index 69914cf..0538a98 100644
--- a/apps/docs/src/renderer/main.tsx
+++ b/apps/docs/src/renderer/main.tsx
@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@ import '@genoffice/ui/ai-scope-quote.css'
